  "description": "Future in the past описывает то, что было будущим относительно некоторого момента в прошлом.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B2-22-RU",
    "lesson_num": 22,
    "title": "Правила: Future in the past",
    "level": "B2",
    "overview": "Future in the past описывает то, что было будущим относительно некоторого момента в прошлом.",
    "main_rule": "Was/were going to = past intention. Would = future from past viewpoint. Was/were about to = immediate future from past viewpoint. Was/were due to = scheduled future from past viewpoint.",
    "form": "was/were going to + V1. would + V1. was/were about to + V1. was/were due to + V1.",
    "when_why": "Главное — past viewpoint: At 9 a.m. I knew that I would finish by noon.",
    "examples": "I was going to call you, but I forgot. → Я собирался тебе позвонить, но забыл.\nHe said he would help. → Он сказал, что поможет.\nWe were about to leave when she arrived. → Мы уже собирались уходить, когда она пришла.\nThe train was due to arrive at noon. → Поезд должен был прибыть в полдень.",
    "special_cases": "Would here is not conditional; it means future relative to past. Do not switch automatically to will after a past reporting verb.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ He said he will help. → ✅ He said he would help.",
    "dont_confuse": "Compare viewpoint now vs then: I will finish. / I knew I would finish.",
    "quick_summary": "Future from past viewpoint:\nwas going to.\nwould.\nwas about to.\nwas due to."
  },
